  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In order to work around the already-reported bug of large video playlists freezing the world for sometimes minutes at a time, I'd like to set a new video URL and have it play immediately after it is loaded.\n\nThe current workaround of delaying a play event is not reliable, because I have no idea how long to delay the play event. The video can take longer to load, perhaps because the entire thing has to be downloaded before it even starts, so it fails depending the video, the network conditions at the time, and other factors out of our control.\n\nThere might be more than one decent solution. Examples:\n\n(a) A different RPC to set the URL and play it immediately. This would be simplest to use.\n\n(b) An \"on video ready\" trigger to let us implement it ourselves. This would be harder to use, but perhaps it would let us display a loading placeholder while the video is loading and then hide it once the real video is ready to go, and some people might want to trigger some other event.",
